WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.480
Those who are branded with a Darksign will live forever.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.860
But is eternal life a blessing

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:07.320
or a curse?

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.860
The theocracy in the land is based around the Way of White,

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.940
which follows the will of lord Gwyn.

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:18.380
Serving under Gwyn are esteemed houses like the house of Thorolund.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:23.100
Think for a moment about what you know of churches that existed in medieval times?

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:26.280
Churches seek control of all people in the name of god.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:28.100
And are conservative by nature.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:29.800
They fear change.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:33.280
One day people become branded with eternal life.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:36.920
This would disrupt the balance and naturally the Church would fear this.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:38.800
But how to deal with it?

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:41.700
Should you label it as a blessing and as the will of God?

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:42.560
No,

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:47.020
if this eternal life ended with people losing the will to live and becoming hollow

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:50.100
then why not label the Darksign as a curse?

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:52.420
We don't know what made the Darksign,

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.220
but the Church made it evil.

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:57.360
So,

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.400
what happens if a member of the Church becomes undead?

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.860
To keep the age of Fire going bonfires can be fed humanity through the Art of Kindling.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:14.060
Hidden deep within the catacombs is rumored to be a technique where bonfires can be fed to grow even stronger.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.920
The Way of White seeks this knowledge to better serve lord Gwyn.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:22.640
The first undead member of the Church was a paladin in golden armor.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:27.780
Equipped with legendary treasures, he set out on the first undead mission of the Way of White.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.200
A mission for the Rite of Kindling.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:35.120
From this point forth all undead within the Church are sent on this same mission.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.380
This serves two purposes.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:43.340
Firstly, if any undead succeeds in retrieving the Rite then the Church will grow more powerful.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:47.420
Secondly, it doesn't matter if the mission ends in failure,

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:50.940
because the Church will have rid themselves of a cursed undead.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:54.460
Rhea is a daughter of the house of Thorolund,

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:57.620
which is inarguably the most prestigious religious family.

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:03.460
However, she becomes undead and even her high birth cannot save her from undergoing the undead mission.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:08.940
So, Rhea is shipped to Lordran with two companions in a futile search for kindling.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.440
Upon arrival Rhea meets Petrus.

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:15.080
Petrus is an undead cleric who resides at Firelink Shrine.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:17.120
He guides undead on their mission.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:19.660
But there's more to this man then it seems.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:23.560
Your first clue comes from the items he has stashed under Firelink Shrine.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:27.280
Your second clue comes from the pardoner.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.380
"Hast thou acquaintance with Petrus of Thorolund?

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:39.220
I wager you two hath likely found much in common.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:44.280
For is he not too drenched in sin…"

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:52.720
Shortly after they arrive, Rhea and her party disappear deep into the catacombs.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:57.140
For a while the player will notice their absence from the game.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:00.400
Eventualy, however, Petrus will return.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:02.680
And he returns alone.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:10.360
"Oh, you again?

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:11.580
Me?

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.340
I've become separated from M'lady.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.320
I've scoured near and far,

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:18.360
but no sight of her…

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:19.700
Where could she have gone?

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:20.680
M'lady…

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.940
To think I swore to protect you with my life…"

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:25.560
He's lying.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:30.120
Petrus will gladly admit to his crimes if you discover the truth through Lautrec.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:33.860
Petrus reveals that he hates the lady for her high birth.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.620
But why did he abandon her?

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.260
Perhaps he doesn't think she's worth it.

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:40.000
Perhaps he is a coward.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:45.120
Or perhaps it is his job to ensure that undead never return from the catacombs.

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:50.100
"Good day!

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:52.060
You look reasonably sane!

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:54.140
What are you doing in the Catacombs?

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.880
Are you a cleric or something?"

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:01.440
"Maiden Thorolund and her followers recently arrived in this land,

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:04.660
but she became stranded deep below the Catacombs.

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:06.680
Her followers either fled,

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.280
or were reduced to hollows…

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:11.340
Leaving Maiden Thorolund

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:12.700
all alone.

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:14.240
Not a bad tip, huh?

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:19.220
A nubile cleric would be replete with humanity…"

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:23.360
Lautrec suggests that you rob the helpless girl of her humanity.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:25.500
She is alone in a dark pit.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:28.640
Surrounded by her hollow friends and no way of escape.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:31.380
"You're no Hollow, are you?

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:32.680
Thank goodness.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:34.420
Please be careful.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:37.560
There are two fierce hollows not far from here.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:39.780
They were once brave knights…

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.820
my former escorts.

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:45.940
Who would let such strong spirits be Hollowed so?

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:48.800
Heavens… Is there nothing…

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:51.200
Nothing at all to be done?"

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:58.080
"Have you spoken with Sir Lautrec?

00:04:58.240 --> 00:04:59.860
Splendid.

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:02.800
In the depths of the Catacombs,

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:05.740
M'lady slipped off the giant's coffin

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:07.180
and into a hole.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:10.000
Her two companions are no longer human.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.060
And the lass weeps in solitude.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:14.040
Right now,

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.720
you could do as you please with her.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:20.820
The poor little purebred is entirely helpless."

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:25.180
"You banished those two hollows, did you?

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:28.820
It pains me to think of the trouble my failings have caused.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:33.280
I am certain that both Vince and Nico are grateful to you.

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:35.380
Thank you so very much."

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:37.780
"Oh, it's you…

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:39.640
You rescued M'lady?

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:42.100
Well, a pity that is,

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:44.320
for it will amount to nothing.

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:46.820
For the little madam is not worth her salt

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:48.940
without her family name."

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:55.240
After everything you find Rhea alone praying in the church.

00:05:56.980 --> 00:05:57.880
"Dear Vince...

00:05:58.660 --> 00:05:59.860
Dear Nico…

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:01.140
Forgive me…

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:05.100
I have lost all those who were close to me.

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:09.380
Perhaps Petrus realized my weakness all along,

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:11.940
and thus made the decision to abandon me.

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:14.200
I can hardly blame him now.

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:16.980
If I do go Hollow,

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:18.760
then finish me off.

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:20.500
I beg of you."

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:23.080
This is where the paths splits.

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:25.680
But both paths end in death.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:28.520
If you do not kill Petrus for abandoning Rhea,

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:29.820
then Rhea will die.

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:33.400
Petrus plays innocent, but if you kill him after her death

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:36.480
you will find her ivory talisman upon his person.

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:39.260
Perhaps Petrus kills Rhea to keep her quiet.

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:41.540
Perhaps he hates her high birth.

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:44.420
Or perhaps disposing of undead is his job.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:47.700
But if you kill Petrus for abandoning Rhea

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:50.160
Then she will not be assassinated.

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:57.980
"By the Lords!

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:00.100
You damn fool!

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:01.680
Enough of you!

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:04.000
Feel the wrath of the gods!"

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:08.320
"Fool…What were you thinking?

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:10.420
Too bad for you,

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:13.960
I'm a wolf in sheep's clothing.

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:23.620
Driven to madness by emotion? So be it.

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:29.440
You'll make a fine hollow! You can waltz in the infernal depths together!

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:38.400
No…

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:41.120
This can't be…

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:43.800
It can't end like this…"

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:49.280
If an undead has a purpose, then they will not hollow.

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:53.840
Rhea will teach you miracles in the church until she has nothing left to teach you.

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:56.880
Shortly after, she loses the will to go on,

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.760
but she continues to pray.

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:03.460
Rhea is a highborn girl who becomes undead.

00:08:03.740 --> 00:08:05.860
She no longer has a place in her homeland

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:07.960
and is cast away to be forgotten.

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:11.780
She does her best but fails to find the secret of Kindling.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:15.680
Betrayed by a man who hates her for a high birth,

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:17.580
tricked by Patches,

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:19.820
lusted after by Lautrec,

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:22.520
and responsible for a death of her friends.

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:24.140
She is rescued by you.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.980
The only one in Lordran who gives her mercy.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:33.020
She repays you with miracles, but she soon teaches you all that she knows and is of no use.

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:36.540
And there are eyes watching.

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:39.880
Channelers are the eyes of Seath

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:41.580
and can be found in many lands.

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:44.380
One of them frequents the Undead Church.

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:47.820
While their motives are largely uncertain

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:51.180
It's known that Seath captures maidens for his experiments.

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:56.220
The channeler spies Rhea as she prays

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:58.680
and takes her to a cell in the Archives.

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:01.980
And that is where Rhea hollows

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:04.020
and spends the rest of her days.

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:21.000
"If I do go Hollow, then finish me off. I beg of you."

